  "provenance": {
    "date": "2026-07-29",
    "issue": 237,
    "source": "Entirely synthetic. Shapes were derived from Kettle's existing synthetic fixtures and deterministic recurrence tests; no private statement values were used.",
    "identity": "Fixture and item IDs combine authored set, base-stratum, family, token and pattern IDs from this file. They never use output order, emitted row ordinals or merchant display text.",
    "merchant_naming": "Real public brands where recognising the merchant is the skill under test, and invented unknowable merchants where declining is the correct answer (#257, decided 30 July 2026). Statements remain wholly synthetic: invented dates, amounts and sequences.",
    "sets_are_held_out": "Each pattern's brand list is split in half: the first six merchants are the development set's, the last six the exam set's, and no merchant appears in both (#317, 2 August 2026). Appended rather than interleaved so the development bed regenerates byte for byte and the diff is the exam alone."
